=== stdout ===
OVERVIEW: List Firebase Crashlytics events for one or more issues.

Memory and storage fields appear only when Firebase includes them for an event.
Frame filter flags imply --frames-only for compact agent input.

USAGE: xcrashlytics events [<options>] [<issue-id>]

ARGUMENTS:
  <issue-id>              Canonical issue id, for example FB-ISSUE_ID.
                          Comma-separated ids are accepted.

OPTIONS:
  --issues <issues>       Comma-separated issue ids, for example FB-a,FB-b.
  --format <format>       Output format: text (default), json, or ndjson.
                          (values: text, json, ndjson; default: text)
  --limit <limit>         Limit to N events per issue (default 10). Not
                          combinable with --latest.
  --user-id <user-id>     Only include events for this exact Firebase user id.
  --since <since>         Only include events since 7d, 24h, 30m, 2w, or all
                          (default: the newest events of the last 90d, the
                          maximum).
  --latest                Fetch only the latest event.
  --frames-only           Only emit frame data for each event.
  --app-frames-only       Only emit frames that look app-owned.
  --no-system-frames      Drop redacted, deduplicated, and known system/SDK
                          frames.
  --crashing-thread-only  Only emit frames of Firebase's crashed thread; warns
                          NO_CRASHED_THREAD when an event has none.
  --breadcrumbs           Include each event's breadcrumbs (Analytics events
                          before the crash); large, user ids redacted. Ignored
                          with frame-only output.
  --dsym <dsym>           A .dSYM bundle, or a directory searched recursively
                          for them, to symbolicate frames of its library (xcrun
                          atos). Repeatable.
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

